  "summary": "Reason reports on three November 2026 local ballot measures concerning ALPRs: York, Maine voters passed a citizen initiative banning ALPRs; League City, Texas voters rejected an advisory measure endorsing 84 Flock cameras, with the mayor pledging to disable them; and Pflugerville, Texas voters approved a charter amendment requiring surveillance oversight policies.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "York voted to pass a citizen-led initiative, effective immediately, that bans ALPRs in the town of more than 14,000",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "We have already voted on city council that if the vote is no, we will have the cameras bagged or disabled within 72 hours of the certification of the vote",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "requires the city council 'to adopt protections governing the collection, use, retention, and oversight of data, facial recognition, and surveillance technologies.'",
      "paragraph_idx": 8
    }
  ],
